# Vite's own convention (loaded automatically by `vite build`'s default production mode, no
# --mode flag needed - the same mechanism .env.example documents for the dev-mode fast loop, just
# the production-mode file instead of .env.local). Committed, not gitignored: none of these values
# are secrets - the public API origin, the public Keycloak issuer URL, and the OIDC client id
# are all meant to be visible to any browser that loads this bundle (the client id is public by
# design, adr/0023 - PKCE proves possession, not a client secret this bundle could even keep
# confidential once shipped to a browser). 8-02's own public deployment target (adr/0026).

VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://chat.reserve-me.ru
VITE_KEYCLOAK_AUTHORITY=https://auth.reserve-me.ru/realms/ago-chat
VITE_KEYCLOAK_CLIENT_ID=ago-console

# 8-06. This deployment's operator credentials are printed on demo-shop1's and demo-shop2's pages for
# anyone to use, which makes every conversation in this console readable by any stranger. Turns on the
# shell's standing notice saying exactly that, to both sides of the demo. Belongs here rather than in
# the code because the same bundle is the real product's console - see src/config.ts. The moment this
# deployment stops being the public demo, delete this line; nothing else has to change.
VITE_PUBLIC_DEMO=true

# 19-03: VITE_FAQ_API_BASE_URL (Ago.Faq.Api's own origin) is deliberately absent here - ago-faq has no
# deployment on this cluster yet. Unset is a supported state (src/config.ts): the AI FAQ
# knowledge-base editor (/settings/faq) shows "not configured" instead of the build failing or the
# rest of the console refusing to boot. Add the line here once ago-faq is actually deployed.
